msgid "Design principles of operator representations {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"
msgstr "Prinsip desain representasi operator {#design-principles-of-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how a [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") is organized and how to work with it: how to build one, how to inspect and combine operators, and how to bring two operators into a form where they can be compared. Start here when you write down a Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menjelaskan bagaimana sebuah [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") disusun dan cara bekerja dengannya: cara membuatnya, cara memeriksa dan menggabungkan operator, serta cara membawa dua operator ke bentuk yang bisa dibandingkan. Mulai dari sini saat kamu menuliskan sebuah Hamiltonian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") is an exact sum of products of bosonic creation and annihilation operators with complex coefficients. It carries no occupation cutoff. A bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many bosons, so its Fock space is infinite-dimensional, and a truncation enters only when the operator is mapped onto qubits (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)). Everything in this guide therefore happens in the exact algebra of the canonical commutation relations,\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") adalah jumlah eksak dari hasil kali operator penciptaan dan pemusnahan bosonik dengan koefisien kompleks. Ia tidak membawa cutoff okupansi. Sebuah mode bosonik bisa menampung boson dalam jumlah sembarang, sehingga ruang Fock-nya berdimensi tak hingga, dan pemotongan baru muncul ketika operator dipetakan ke qubit (lihat [Memotong ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)). Karena itu, semua yang ada di panduan ini terjadi dalam aljabar eksak dari relasi komutasi kanonik,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[b_i, b_j^\\dagger] = \\delta_{ij}, \\qquad [b_i, b_j] = [b_i^\\dagger, b_j^\\dagger] = 0 \\, .\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[b_i, b_j^\\dagger] = \\delta_{ij}, \\qquad [b_i, b_j] = [b_i^\\dagger, b_j^\\dagger] = 0 \\, .\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two consequences shape the interface. A mode index can repeat within a single term, because $b_i^\\dagger b_i^\\dagger$ is a valid operator that creates two bosons. Also, reordering two factors never introduces a sign, although moving an annihilation operator past a creation operator on the same mode adds a term, $b_i b_i^\\dagger = b_i^\\dagger b_i + 1$.\n"
msgstr "Dua konsekuensi membentuk antarmukanya. Indeks mode bisa berulang dalam satu suku, karena $b_i^\\dagger b_i^\\dagger$ adalah operator yang valid yang menciptakan dua boson. Selain itu, menukar urutan dua faktor tidak pernah memunculkan tanda, walaupun memindahkan operator pemusnahan melewati operator penciptaan pada mode yang sama menambah satu suku, $b_i b_i^\\dagger = b_i^\\dagger b_i + 1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Storage {#storage}"
msgstr "Penyimpanan {#storage}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator keeps its terms in four flat arrays, similar to the compressed sparse row format of a sparse matrix:\n"
msgstr "Sebuah operator menyimpan suku-sukunya dalam empat array datar, mirip dengan format compressed sparse row pada matriks jarang:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|              |                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `coeffs`     | One complex coefficient per term.                                                       |\n"
"| `actions`    | One boolean per factor: `True` for a creation and `False` for an annihilation operator. |\n"
"| `modes`      | One mode index per factor.                                                              |\n"
"| `boundaries` | The positions in `actions` and `modes` where each term starts and ends.                 |\n"
msgstr ""
"|              |                                                                                         |\n"
"| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `coeffs`     | Satu koefisien kompleks per suku.                                                       |\n"
"| `actions`    | Satu boolean per faktor: `True` untuk operator penciptaan dan `False` untuk pemusnahan. |\n"
"| `modes`      | Satu indeks mode per faktor.                                                            |\n"
"| `boundaries` | Posisi di `actions` dan `modes` tempat setiap suku dimulai dan berakhir.                |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The constructor takes these four arrays directly. The operator below has three terms, namely $2 b_0^\\dagger b_1$, $-i b_1^\\dagger b_1^\\dagger$, and the constant $0.5$, and you can read the arrays back with the `get_*` methods:\n"
msgstr "Konstruktor menerima keempat array ini secara langsung. Operator di bawah punya tiga suku, yaitu $2 b_0^\\dagger b_1$, $-i b_1^\\dagger b_1^\\dagger$, dan konstanta $0.5$, dan kamu bisa membaca kembali array-nya dengan method `get_*`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first term spans positions 0 to 2 of `actions` and `modes`, the second spans 2 to 4, and the third spans 4 to 4, which is how the constant term, a term without factors, is stored. The repeated mode `1` in the second term is preserved as written; a term is never dropped or merged because a mode index appears twice.\n"
msgstr "Suku pertama mencakup posisi 0 sampai 2 dari `actions` dan `modes`, suku kedua mencakup 2 sampai 4, dan suku ketiga mencakup 4 sampai 4, begitulah suku konstanta, yaitu suku tanpa faktor, disimpan. Mode `1` yang berulang di suku kedua dipertahankan seperti yang ditulis; sebuah suku tidak pernah dibuang atau digabung hanya karena indeks mode muncul dua kali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  An operator built with [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") does not store its terms in the order of the dictionary, so its arrays can list the terms in a different order from run to run. The operator itself is the same, and nothing below that compares or prints operators depends on the stored order.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Operator yang dibuat dengan [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\") tidak menyimpan suku-sukunya menurut urutan dictionary, sehingga array-nya bisa mencantumkan suku dalam urutan berbeda dari satu run ke run lain. Operatornya sendiri tetap sama, dan tidak ada hal di bawah ini yang membandingkan atau mencetak operator yang bergantung pada urutan penyimpanan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The layout makes construction and arithmetic cheap, with one consequence: an operator can hold the same term several times at once. Sums and products append terms and do not merge them, so call [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") when you need unique terms (see [Do arithmetic](#operators-arithmetic)).\n"
msgstr "Tata letak ini membuat konstruksi dan aritmetika murah, dengan satu konsekuensi: sebuah operator bisa memuat suku yang sama beberapa kali sekaligus. Penjumlahan dan perkalian menambahkan suku tanpa menggabungkannya, jadi panggil [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") saat kamu butuh suku yang unik (lihat [Melakukan aritmetika](#operators-arithmetic)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build operators {#build-operators}"
msgstr "Membuat operator {#build-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The most direct way to build an operator is [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\"), which takes a dictionary from a tuple of factors to a coefficient. The functions [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-cre#qiskit_bosons.operators.cre \"qiskit_bosons.operators.cre\") and [`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-ann#qiskit_bosons.operators.ann \"qiskit_bosons.operators.ann\") create the factors, and the empty tuple is the constant term:\n"
msgstr "Cara paling langsung untuk membuat operator adalah [`from_dict()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_dict\"), yang menerima dictionary dari tuple faktor ke koefisien. Fungsi [`cre()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-cre#qiskit_bosons.operators.cre \"qiskit_bosons.operators.cre\") dan [`ann()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-ann#qiskit_bosons.operators.ann \"qiskit_bosons.operators.ann\") membuat faktor-faktornya, dan tuple kosong adalah suku konstanta:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the printed form, `+0` stands for $b_0^\\dagger$ and `-0` for $b_0$. The constructors [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\") and [`one()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one\") return the additive and the multiplicative identity, and [`from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms\") rebuilds an operator from the iterator of [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms\").\n"
msgstr "Pada bentuk cetak, `+0` mewakili $b_0^\\dagger$ dan `-0` mewakili $b_0$. Konstruktor [`zero()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.zero\") dan [`one()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.one\") mengembalikan identitas aditif dan multiplikatif, dan [`from_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.from_terms\") membangun ulang operator dari iterator [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.iter_terms\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The operator library provides the dimensionless position and momentum quadratures,\n"
msgstr "Library operator menyediakan kuadratur posisi dan momentum tanpa dimensi,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{q} = \\frac{b^\\dagger + b}{\\sqrt{2}}, \\qquad\n"
"\\hat{p} = \\frac{i \\left(b^\\dagger - b\\right)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{q} = \\frac{b^\\dagger + b}{\\sqrt{2}}, \\qquad\n"
"\\hat{p} = \\frac{i \\left(b^\\dagger - b\\right)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "as [`position()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-position#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position\") and [`momentum()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-momentum#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum\"). Together with the commutator functions of the same module, you can check the algebra directly:\n"
msgstr "sebagai [`position()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-position#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.position\") dan [`momentum()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-momentum#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.momentum\"). Bersama fungsi komutator dari modul yang sama, kamu bisa memeriksa aljabarnya secara langsung:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The module also provides [`anti_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-anti-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator\") and [`double_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-double-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator\"). All three take operators of the same type and return a new operator.\n"
msgstr "Modul ini juga menyediakan [`anti_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-anti-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.anti_commutator\") dan [`double_commutator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-library-double-commutator#qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.library.double_commutator\"). Ketiganya menerima operator bertipe sama dan mengembalikan operator baru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operators-product-order\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mind the order of a product {#mind-the-order-of-a-product}"
msgstr "Perhatikan urutan sebuah hasil kali {#mind-the-order-of-a-product}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two operators can be multiplied in two ways, and they are easy to confuse. The `@` operator is the mathematical product, so `a @ b` is $AB$. The `&` operator is *composition*, which follows Qiskit’s convention of reading from left to right: `a & b` first applies `a` and then `b`, so it is $BA$. The commutator functions use `@`, so `commutator(a, b)` is $[A, B]$. Building the bracket yourself out of `&` silently negates it:\n"
msgstr "Dua operator bisa dikalikan dengan dua cara, dan keduanya mudah tertukar. Operator `@` adalah hasil kali matematis, jadi `a @ b` adalah $AB$. Operator `&` adalah *komposisi*, yang mengikuti konvensi Qiskit dengan membaca dari kiri ke kanan: `a & b` menerapkan `a` lebih dulu lalu `b`, jadi hasilnya $BA$. Fungsi komutator memakai `@`, jadi `commutator(a, b)` adalah $[A, B]$. Kalau kamu membangun sendiri braket itu dengan `&`, tandanya diam-diam terbalik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect an operator {#inspect-an-operator}"
msgstr "Memeriksa operator {#inspect-an-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator is not directly iterable, because its terms live in the flat arrays above. Use [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") instead, which yields a list of `(is_creation, mode)` pairs and a coefficient for each term. The iterator returns copies, so changing them does not change the operator.\n"
msgstr "Operator tidak bisa diiterasi secara langsung, karena suku-sukunya berada di array datar di atas. Gunakan [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") sebagai gantinya, yang menghasilkan daftar pasangan `(is_creation, mode)` dan sebuah koefisien untuk setiap suku. Iterator mengembalikan salinan, jadi mengubahnya tidak mengubah operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Several methods summarize the structure of an operator:\n"
msgstr "Beberapa method merangkum struktur sebuah operator:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`get_support()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support\") is the set of modes the operator acts on, [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") is the smallest register that can hold it, and [`max_rank()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank\") is the length of its longest term.\n"
msgstr "[`get_support()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.get_support\") adalah himpunan mode yang dikenai operator, [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") adalah register terkecil yang bisa memuatnya, dan [`max_rank()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.max_rank\") adalah panjang suku terpanjangnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  A **mode** is an abstract index that labels one bosonic degree of freedom. It has no meaning of its own: you determine which site of a lattice, which vibrational coordinate or which optical port a mode stands for. The [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") uses the same indices (see [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), so an operator and the gates that carry it agree on what mode `2` is without either one knowing what it represents. Nothing in the operator fixes how many levels a mode has, which is also why the register size is only a lower bound; [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") is the smallest register that holds the operator, not a property of it.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Sebuah **mode** adalah indeks abstrak yang melabeli satu derajat kebebasan bosonik. Indeks ini tidak punya makna sendiri: kamu yang menentukan situs lattice mana, koordinat vibrasi mana, atau port optik mana yang diwakili sebuah mode. [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") memakai indeks yang sama (lihat [Bekerja dengan bosonic circuit](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), sehingga operator dan gate yang membawanya sepakat tentang apa itu mode `2` tanpa salah satunya tahu apa yang diwakilinya. Tidak ada di dalam operator yang menetapkan berapa level yang dimiliki sebuah mode, dan itu juga sebabnya ukuran register hanyalah batas bawah; [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\") adalah register terkecil yang memuat operator, bukan properti operator itu.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The occupation methods report how many bosons a single term can place in one mode. This is a lower bound on the cutoff that a mapping needs. It is not a sufficient cutoff, because repeated applications of the operator, as in a time evolution, can populate higher levels (see [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation)):\n"
msgstr "Method okupansi melaporkan berapa banyak boson yang bisa ditempatkan satu suku di satu mode. Ini adalah batas bawah untuk cutoff yang dibutuhkan sebuah pemetaan. Ini bukan cutoff yang cukup, karena penerapan operator berulang kali, seperti pada evolusi waktu, bisa mengisi level yang lebih tinggi (lihat [Memotong ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation)):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two further checks look at conserved quantities. An operator conserves the particle number when every term has as many creation as annihilation operators. Passing a list of block sizes tests the same condition within each block of consecutive modes:\n"
msgstr "Dua pemeriksaan lain melihat besaran yang kekal. Sebuah operator mengekalkan jumlah partikel jika setiap suku punya operator penciptaan sebanyak operator pemusnahan. Memberikan daftar ukuran blok menguji kondisi yang sama di dalam setiap blok mode yang berurutan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, [`relabel_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes\") renames modes: mode `i` becomes `permutation[i]`. The list must be long enough to index every mode of the operator and must not repeat an entry:\n"
msgstr "Terakhir, [`relabel_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.relabel_modes\") mengganti nama mode: mode `i` menjadi `permutation[i]`. Daftarnya harus cukup panjang untuk mengindeks setiap mode operator dan tidak boleh mengulang entri:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"operators-arithmetic\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Do arithmetic {#do-arithmetic}"
msgstr "Melakukan aritmetika {#do-arithmetic}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operators support addition, subtraction, negation, and multiplication and division by a number, in the usual operator form or in place:\n"
msgstr "Operator mendukung penjumlahan, pengurangan, negasi, serta perkalian dan pembagian dengan sebuah angka, dalam bentuk operator biasa atau in place:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The three terms of `total` were never merged, so the operator held `b_dag` twice until [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") combined them. The method sums the coefficients of identical terms and drops those whose total magnitude is below a tolerance. It is a structural operation: it compares the written factors and does *not* apply the commutation relations. The related method [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") removes small coefficients in place without merging first, so call [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") before [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") when an operator can hold duplicate terms.\n"
msgstr "Ketiga suku `total` tidak pernah digabung, jadi operator memuat `b_dag` dua kali sampai [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") menggabungkannya. Method ini menjumlahkan koefisien suku-suku yang identik dan membuang suku yang total magnitudonya di bawah toleransi. Ini adalah operasi struktural: ia membandingkan faktor-faktor seperti yang tertulis dan *tidak* menerapkan relasi komutasi. Method terkait [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") menghapus koefisien kecil in place tanpa menggabungkan dulu, jadi panggil [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") sebelum [`ichop()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.ichop\") ketika operator bisa memuat suku duplikat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Products use `@` or `&` as described above, and `**` raises an operator to an integer power:\n"
msgstr "Hasil kali memakai `@` atau `&` seperti dijelaskan di atas, dan `**` memangkatkan operator dengan bilangan bulat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result lists the four orderings as written. Reducing them to a single form needs the commutation relations, which the next section applies.\n"
msgstr "Hasilnya mencantumkan keempat urutan seperti yang tertulis. Menyederhanakannya ke satu bentuk membutuhkan relasi komutasi, yang diterapkan di bagian berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The adjoint reverses the order of the factors in each term, exchanges creation and annihilation operators, and conjugates the coefficients. The method [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") tests whether an operator equals its adjoint:\n"
msgstr "Adjoint membalik urutan faktor di setiap suku, menukar operator penciptaan dan pemusnahan, dan mengonjugasi koefisien. Method [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") menguji apakah sebuah operator sama dengan adjoint-nya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A lone hopping term is not Hermitian, which matters when you group terms for a time evolution: each group must be Hermitian on its own (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)).\n"
msgstr "Satu suku hopping saja tidak Hermitian, dan ini penting saat kamu mengelompokkan suku untuk evolusi waktu: setiap kelompok harus Hermitian dengan sendirinya (lihat [Mengelompokkan suku operator: memanfaatkan struktur operator](grouping#grouping-explanation)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normal order and compare operators {#normal-order-and-compare-operators}"
msgstr "Urutan normal dan membandingkan operator {#normal-order-and-compare-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two products of ladder operators can be the same operator and still look different, because $b\\,b^\\dagger$ and $b^\\dagger b + 1$ are equal in the algebra. Operators that are equal in this sense need not be stored equally, so comparing them needs the commutation relations. The method [`normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered\") applies them: it moves every creation operator to the left of every annihilation operator and adds a term whenever a pair on the same mode is exchanged.\n"
msgstr "Dua hasil kali operator tangga bisa merupakan operator yang sama namun terlihat berbeda, karena $b\\,b^\\dagger$ dan $b^\\dagger b + 1$ sama di dalam aljabar. Operator yang sama dalam arti ini belum tentu disimpan dengan cara yang sama, jadi membandingkannya membutuhkan relasi komutasi. Method [`normal_ordered()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.normal_ordered\") menerapkannya: ia memindahkan setiap operator penciptaan ke kiri semua operator pemusnahan dan menambah satu suku setiap kali sepasang operator pada mode yang sama ditukar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ordered operator is returned as an unmerged sum, with five stored terms that reduce to three after [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") merges them. Normal ordering never makes a term vanish: $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger$ and every other repeated factor stay.\n"
msgstr "Operator yang sudah diurutkan dikembalikan sebagai jumlah yang belum digabung, dengan lima suku tersimpan yang berkurang menjadi tiga setelah [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.simplify\") menggabungkannya. Pengurutan normal tidak pernah membuat suku lenyap: $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger$ dan setiap faktor berulang lainnya tetap ada.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `sandwich` argument sets how the modes inside the two groups of factors are arranged. By default both groups are sorted in descending order. With `sandwich=True`, the creation operators are ascending and the annihilation operators descending, which puts the larger indices towards the middle:\n"
msgstr "Argumen `sandwich` menentukan bagaimana mode di dalam kedua kelompok faktor disusun. Secara bawaan kedua kelompok diurutkan menurun. Dengan `sandwich=True`, operator penciptaan menaik dan operator pemusnahan menurun, sehingga indeks yang lebih besar berada di tengah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `==` operator tests exact equality of the stored terms, with no tolerance and no simplification, so it can report a difference between two operators that are mathematically equal. The method [`equiv()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv\") brings the difference of the two operators to normal order first and then tests that every coefficient is below a tolerance. It is the comparison you almost always want:\n"
msgstr "Operator `==` menguji kesamaan eksak dari suku-suku yang tersimpan, tanpa toleransi dan tanpa penyederhanaan, jadi ia bisa melaporkan perbedaan antara dua operator yang secara matematis sama. Method [`equiv()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.equiv\") lebih dulu membawa selisih kedua operator ke urutan normal, lalu menguji bahwa setiap koefisien berada di bawah toleransi. Inilah perbandingan yang hampir selalu kamu inginkan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method `simplify` alone leaves the two forms apart, because it merges only identical written terms. Likewise, [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") compares an operator with its adjoint in normal order, so it recognizes $b\\,b^\\dagger + b^\\dagger b$ as Hermitian without further work.\n"
msgstr "Method `simplify` saja membiarkan kedua bentuk itu tetap terpisah, karena ia hanya menggabungkan suku yang tertulis identik. Demikian pula, [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\") membandingkan operator dengan adjoint-nya dalam urutan normal, sehingga ia mengenali $b\\,b^\\dagger + b^\\dagger b$ sebagai Hermitian tanpa usaha tambahan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Normal ordering is an exact identity in the untruncated algebra, and `equiv` relies on that. It is *not* an identity after a truncation. A mapped operator depends on the form you map, so the mapped images of `contracted` and `reordered` above differ, on the highest retained level only. See [Truncate the Fock space](mappers#truncation-explanation) for the size of the difference and how to choose a form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Catatan\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Pengurutan normal adalah identitas eksak dalam aljabar yang tidak dipotong, dan `equiv` bergantung pada hal itu. Ini *bukan* identitas setelah pemotongan. Operator yang dipetakan bergantung pada bentuk yang kamu petakan, jadi citra terpetakan dari `contracted` dan `reordered` di atas berbeda, hanya pada level tertinggi yang dipertahankan. Lihat [Memotong ruang Fock](mappers#truncation-explanation) untuk besar perbedaannya dan cara memilih bentuk.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Order and filter terms {#order-and-filter-terms}"
msgstr "Mengurutkan dan memfilter suku {#order-and-filter-terms}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reordering the *terms* of an operator, as opposed to the factors inside a term, does not change the operator but can change the behavior of algorithms that read the terms in order, such as a randomized product formula. The functions of [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") return a new operator and keep any group indices attached to their terms.\n"
msgstr "Mengurutkan ulang *suku-suku* sebuah operator, berbeda dari faktor di dalam satu suku, tidak mengubah operatornya tetapi bisa mengubah perilaku algoritma yang membaca suku secara berurutan, seperti product formula teracak. Fungsi-fungsi di [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") mengembalikan operator baru dan mempertahankan indeks kelompok yang melekat pada suku-sukunya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`canonical_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-canonical-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order\") sorts the terms into a fixed order that depends only on the written factors, so an operator reads the same no matter how it was assembled. [`order_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-order-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms\") sorts by a key that you supply, which receives each term as the tuple that [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\") yields:\n"
msgstr "[`canonical_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-canonical-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.canonical_order\") mengurutkan suku ke dalam urutan tetap yang hanya bergantung pada faktor yang tertulis, sehingga operator terbaca sama bagaimanapun ia dirakit. [`order_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-order-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.order_terms\") mengurutkan menurut kunci yang kamu berikan, yang menerima setiap suku sebagai tuple yang dihasilkan [`iter_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait.iter_terms\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If an operator carries group indices (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)), the function [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") makes each group one contiguous run of terms:\n"
msgstr "Jika sebuah operator membawa indeks kelompok (lihat [Mengelompokkan suku operator: memanfaatkan struktur operator](grouping#grouping-explanation)), fungsi [`group_order()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-group-order#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.group_order\") membuat setiap kelompok menjadi satu rangkaian suku yang berurutan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last helper removes terms rather than reordering them. A term that is a product of number operators, $b_i^\\dagger b_i$, only multiplies each Fock state by a phase, so [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") can drop the constant, the number operators, and their products when that phase is irrelevant for what you compute. It changes the operator *in place* and requires a normal-ordered operator, which it does not check:\n"
msgstr "Helper terakhir menghapus suku, bukan mengurutkannya ulang. Suku yang merupakan hasil kali operator bilangan, $b_i^\\dagger b_i$, hanya mengalikan setiap state Fock dengan fase, jadi [`filter_diagonal_terms()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms-filter-diagonal-terms#qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms.filter_diagonal_terms\") bisa membuang konstanta, operator bilangan, dan hasil kalinya ketika fase itu tidak relevan untuk apa yang kamu hitung. Fungsi ini mengubah operator *in place* dan membutuhkan operator yang sudah berurutan normal, yang tidak diperiksanya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only the two hopping terms remain. The on-site interaction and the number operator are diagonal in the occupation basis, so they are removed together with the constant. The repeated mode in the interaction is handled correctly: $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0 b_0$ is diagonal, while $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0$ would not be.\n"
msgstr "Hanya dua suku hopping yang tersisa. Interaksi on-site dan operator bilangan bersifat diagonal pada basis okupansi, jadi keduanya dihapus bersama konstanta. Mode berulang pada interaksi ditangani dengan benar: $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0 b_0$ diagonal, sedangkan $b_0^\\dagger b_0^\\dagger b_0$ tidak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah berikutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation) shows how to tag terms with group indices.\n"
msgstr "[Mengelompokkan suku operator: memanfaatkan struktur operator](grouping#grouping-explanation) menunjukkan cara memberi tag pada suku dengan indeks kelompok.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation) turns an operator into a qubit operator, including the choice of encoding and the effect of a truncation.\n"
msgstr "[Petakan representasi operator](mappers#mappers-explanation) mengubah operator menjadi operator qubit, termasuk pilihan encoding dan efek pemotongan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) places an operator into a circuit as an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate.\n"
msgstr "[Bekerja dengan bosonic circuit](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) menempatkan operator ke dalam circuit sebagai gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) builds the Hamiltonian of a Bose-Hubbard chain and simulates it end to end.\n"
msgstr "[Simulasikan dinamika Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started) membangun Hamiltonian rantai Bose-Hubbard dan mensimulasikannya dari awal sampai akhir.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`qiskit_bosons.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") and [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") modules document the complete interface.\n"
msgstr "Modul [`qiskit_bosons.operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\") dan [`qiskit_bosons.operators.terms`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-terms#module-qiskit_bosons.operators.terms \"qiskit_bosons.operators.terms\") mendokumentasikan antarmuka secara lengkap.\n"
